<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

	<!--
		Reptilian gene. Pure-XML parts: a modest sharp armour offset and a +10 C minimum
		comfortable temperature (cold-blooded: the whole comfort band shifts up).

		Cold is survivable for her (built 2026-09-30). The +10 puts her comfort band at 26 C
		and up, and her SAFE band - comfort widened by 10 degrees either way - starts at 16 C,
		which is under the air on nearly every map. Vanilla's hypothermia giver adds severity
		below 16 and only sheds it above 26, so a reptile used to accumulate a hypothermia she
		could never get rid of, and die of it. The two immunity fields below end that: she
		cannot catch Hypothermia at all, which also closes vanilla's frostbite path (it rolls
		below 0 C only while hypothermia is past 0.37 severity), and PMM_Hediff_ColdTorpor
		takes its place - she slows, then sleeps, and wakes once she is warm again.
		Source/Reptiles/ColdTorpor.cs carries the rates and the reasoning.

		C# parts: PMM_Reptiles.Gene_Reptile adds/removes the hidden PMM_Hediff_Shedding
		hediff in PostAdd/PostRemove (the slime-gel oozing pattern); the hediff's comp
		drops a stack of PMM_ReptileScale once a year.

		VEF part: the GeneExtension modExtension attaches PMM_Hediff_EggLaying to the
		whole body, whose VEF.Genes.HediffCompProperties_HumanEggLayer replaces live
		birth with a single fertilized egg (the Alpha Genes AG_EggLaying pattern).

		Endogenes-only, not in the tradeable gene pool (same ruling as the slime gel gene).
	-->
	<GeneDef>
		<defName>PMM_Gene_Reptile</defName>
		<!-- One family per woman (user ruling 2026-10-01). The identity genes of the
		     three families - the reptilian, the insectoid (PMM_Gene_Insect) and the
		     slime gel (PMM_Gene_SlimeGel) - share the tag below, so the engine treats
		     any two of them as conflicting: the loser is greyed out when both land on
		     one pawn, the xenotype and xenogerm editors refuse to build the mix, and
		     core's `RemoveConflictingGenes` (removal by shared tag) takes the old
		     family's gene off a woman remade into another family. The tag string is
		     never shown to the player; the UI names the gene that won. -->
		<exclusionTags>
			<li>PMM_MamonoFamily</li>
		</exclusionTags>
		<label>reptilian</label>
		<labelShortAdj>reptilian</labelShortAdj>
		<description>Carriers of this gene have the cold-blooded body of a reptile mamono: tough scales that blunt cuts and claws, a warmth-loving disposition, and a body that lays a single egg rather than birthing live young. Cold does not kill her - it slows her, and then sends her into a torpor she sleeps off once she is warm again. Once a year she sheds her old scales, which can be worked like fine leather.</description>
		<iconPath>UI/Icons/Genes/PMM_Gene_Reptile</iconPath>
		<geneClass>PMM_Reptiles.Gene_Reptile</geneClass>
		<displayCategory>Miscellaneous</displayCategory>
		<canGenerateInGeneSet>false</canGenerateInGeneSet>
		<biostatCpx>2</biostatCpx>
		<biostatMet>1</biostatMet>
		<statOffsets>
			<!-- Modest sharp resistance (locked ruling). -->
			<ArmorRating_Sharp>0.15</ArmorRating_Sharp>
			<!-- Cold-blooded: comfortable band shifted 10 degrees warmer. Her safe minimum is
			     therefore 16 C, and that is the temperature the cold torpor builds below. -->
			<ComfyTemperatureMin>10</ComfyTemperatureMin>
		</statOffsets>
		<!-- Cannot catch the cold at all (2026-09-30): no Hypothermia, and no frostbite
		     injury either, since vanilla rolls those below 0 C only while hypothermia is
		     past 0.37 severity. PMM_Hediff_ColdTorpor takes its place - the giver and the
		     hediff are in Source/Reptiles/ColdTorpor.cs and Hediffs_ColdTorpor.xml. -->
		<makeImmuneTo>
			<li>Hypothermia</li>
		</makeImmuneTo>
		<hediffGiversCannotGive>
			<li>Hypothermia</li>
		</hediffGiversCannotGive>
		<modExtensions>
			<li Class="VEF.Genes.GeneExtension">
				<hediffToWholeBody>PMM_Hediff_EggLaying</hediffToWholeBody>
			</li>
		</modExtensions>
	</GeneDef>

	<!--
		Lamia tail gene. Two parts:
		1. Tail-grapple ability through the vanilla gene-granted-ability block (the
		   Dorome mud-merge / Genie wish pattern): the comp effect drags the victim
		   adjacent and applies PMM_Hediff_Constricted. No custom gene class needed.
		2. The serpent body, via Big & Small. This follows B&S's own snake-tail gene
		   (LoS_Snake_Tail in BigSmall_Genes): a PawnExtension with thingDefSwap
		   aimed at BS_Naga. The race fuser then gives the pawn the BS_SnakeHuman
		   body and applies BS's BS_Naga_Race tracker, which brings the serpent
		   metabolism package (eats rarely, slithers slower).
		   exclusionTags (taur, Tail) keep it from stacking with other lower-body
		   swaps, same as the B&S gene.

		The tail GRAPHIC comes from the BS_Naga_Race tracker and nothing else. The
		tracker holds the BS_SnekGraphicSet tail node. The fuser keeps the swap
		target's RaceExtension on the fused def, so that tracker lands on the pawn
		and draws the tail. The tracker blanks its own tail when the pawn carries a
		gene tagged "taur", so the Flagger below raises ShowBaseAbdomen and the
		drawing continues. Whole recipe: thingDefSwap + Flagger + renderCacheOff.

		Do NOT add a render hediff here again. A second renderer draws the same
		textures twice. PMM_Hediff_LamiaTailRender was deleted on 2026-09-20 once
		the wing cleanup proved a B&S tracker draws a gene-swapped body on its own.
	-->
	<GeneDef>
		<defName>PMM_Gene_LamiaTail</defName>
		<label>lamia tail</label>
		<labelShortAdj>lamia-tailed</labelShortAdj>
		<description>Carriers of this gene have the long, powerful serpent tail of a lamia. In a fight she can lash out with it, drag an opponent into her coils, and constrict them while she teases their will away.</description>
		<iconPath>UI/Icons/Genes/PMM_Gene_LamiaTail</iconPath>
		<displayCategory>Miscellaneous</displayCategory>
		<canGenerateInGeneSet>false</canGenerateInGeneSet>
		<biostatCpx>1</biostatCpx>
		<biostatMet>1</biostatMet>
		<exclusionTags>
			<li>taur</li>
			<li>Tail</li>
		</exclusionTags>
		<abilities>
			<li>PMM_Ability_TailGrapple</li>
		</abilities>
		<modExtensions>
			<li Class="BigAndSmall.PawnExtension">
				<!-- The tail is taller than the render atlas, so it would be cropped
				     without this. The naga tracker sets the same flag on itself. -->
				<renderCacheOff>true</renderCacheOff>
				<thingDefSwap>BS_Naga</thingDefSwap>
			</li>
			<!-- Same as B&S's snake-tail gene: raise ShowBaseAbdomen so the tracker
			     stops blanking its own tail art for taur-tagged genes. This flag is
			     what makes the tail show. There is no PMM render hediff any more. -->
			<li Class="BigAndSmall.Flagger"><flags><ShowBaseAbdomen/></flags></li>
		</modExtensions>
	</GeneDef>

</Defs>
